# Owner standing instructions

1. Read `docs/OWNER_STANDING.md` (repo root) for lasting owner working preferences. Do **not** rely on chat memory alone.
2. When the user states a **lasting** preference about how agents must work (not a one-off task), **update `docs/OWNER_STANDING.md` in the same session** (edit the matching section + changelog line). Tool-specific board details go in their standing board file; product/tech decisions go in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
3. If that preference is a **reusable workflow** (implementation day loop, closeout order, CI/CD gates, final reply shape, standing↔factory upstream), also propose the generic version upstream to the factory as a pull request — especially changes to `software-factory-all-in-one/08-IMPLEMENTATION-DAY.md`, `software-factory-all-in-one/09-CI-CD.md`, and `software-factory-all-in-one/templates/docs/OWNER_STANDING.md` — in the same session; never edit the vendored folder in place.
4. After updating standing docs, keep local default branch ↔ origin mirrored per OWNER_STANDING / AGENTS Git Safety.


